From cc01b2298aec8bf692d61f41a896f76dc62ab643 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:38:40 -0500
Subject: [RFC PATCH 3/3] Input: pm8xxx-vibrator - replace drive bits when
 intensity changes

reg_vib_drv caches the previous drive field. ORing a new level into this
value retains old bits when intensity changes without first stopping the
effect. For example, changing drive code 24 to 17 programs code 25.

Clear the old drive field before inserting the new level, preserving the
unrelated register bits. This lets an active effect decrease its drive
strength as requested.

Fixes: 11205bb63e5c ("Input: add support for pm8xxx based vibrator driver")
---
 drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
index e1d69089d4bd..d4fdb5652584 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
@@ -107,7 +107,8 @@ static int pm8xxx_vib_set(struct pm8xxx_vib *vib, bool on)
 		vib->level /= VIB_PER_STEP_mV(vib);
 
 	if (on)
-		val |= (vib->level << regs->drv_shift) & regs->drv_mask;
+		val = (val & ~regs->drv_mask) |
+		      ((vib->level << regs->drv_shift) & regs->drv_mask);
 	else
 		val &= ~regs->drv_mask;
 
